cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ASCENT: Accelerated Single-Cell ENhancer-Target Gene Linking"
abstract: >-
  ASCENT is a high-performance Rcpp/C++ reimplementation of the SCENT algorithm
  for linking cis-regulatory elements (ATAC-seq peaks) to their target genes
  from single-cell multimodal (RNA + ATAC) data. It uses Poisson or negative
  binomial regression with either a Wald test (adaptive bootstrap) or a fast
  analytic score test, parallelized across peak-gene pairs with OpenMP.
type: software
